    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Visual Arts</span> are art forms that produce works primarily visual in nature — created through the conscious expression of skill and imagination. They encompass everything from painting and sculpture to textiles and graphic design.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Visual Arts</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Visual arts are consciously created through the expression of skill or imagination, involving the skillful use of materials for human use and pleasure. They communicate ideas, emotions, and culture through visual means.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Classification of Visual Arts</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Definition</th><th>Examples</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Fine Arts</strong></td><td>Art created primarily for aesthetic purposes</td><td>Drawing, Painting, Sculpture</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Applied Arts</strong></td><td>Art applied to functional/commercial objects</td><td>Graphics, Textile Design, Ceramics</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Fine Arts in Detail</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Drawing:</strong> Creating images using lines and marks on a surface.</li>\n  <li><strong>Painting:</strong> Applying pigment to a surface to create images or abstract works.</li>\n  <li><strong>Sculpture:</strong> Creating three-dimensional forms by carving, modelling, casting, or assembling.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Applied Arts in Detail</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Graphics:</strong> Visual communication through typography, illustration, and layout.</li>\n  <li><strong>Textile Design:</strong> Creating patterns and designs on fabric through weaving, printing, or dyeing.</li>\n  <li><strong>Ceramics:</strong> Making objects from clay fired at high temperatures — pottery, tiles, etc.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Visual arts = skillful use of materials for human use and pleasure. Two main categories: Fine Arts (Drawing, Painting, Sculpture) — primarily aesthetic; Applied Arts (Graphics, Textiles, Ceramics) — functional and aesthetic. Know specific examples of each.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Visual arts are consciously created through skill and imagination. Fine Arts: Drawing, Painting, Sculpture (mainly aesthetic). Applied Arts: Graphics, Textiles, Ceramics (functional + aesthetic).\n</div>\n  ",
