    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Visual arts open up a wide range of <span class=\"learn-keyword\">professional careers</span>. From creative and technical fields to scientific and investigative applications, art skills are in demand across many sectors of the economy.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Creative and Commercial Professions</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Profession</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Graphic Designer</td><td>Creates visual content for print and digital media (logos, layouts, posters, packaging)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Video Editor</td><td>Edits and assembles video footage for films, TV, YouTube, and advertising</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Cartoonist</td><td>Creates cartoon characters and comic illustrations for media and entertainment</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Textile Designer</td><td>Creates patterns and designs for fabric, clothing, and interior decoration</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Painter</td><td>Creates paintings using various media (oil, acrylic, watercolour) for galleries, commissions</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Sculptor</td><td>Creates three-dimensional artworks from stone, metal, clay, wood, or other materials</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Ceramicist</td><td>Makes objects from clay — functional pottery and decorative ceramic artworks</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Photographer</td><td>Captures images using cameras for news, fashion, advertising, portraiture, or documentation</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Applied and Technical Professions</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Cultural Officer:</strong> Works in government agencies to preserve, promote, and manage cultural heritage and arts.</li>\n  <li><strong>Medical Illustrator:</strong> Creates detailed, accurate scientific illustrations of anatomical structures, medical procedures, and biological concepts for textbooks, research, and medical communication.</li>\n  <li><strong>Investigative Illustrator:</strong> Creates visual reconstructions of crime scenes, suspects (facial composites), and events for law enforcement and legal proceedings.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Know all 11 professions with their descriptions: Graphic Designer, Video Editor, Cartoonist, Textile Designer, Painter, Sculptor, Ceramicist, Photographer, Cultural Officer, Medical Illustrator, Investigative Illustrator. Medical illustrator draws anatomical/medical content; Investigative illustrator draws suspect faces and crime scenes.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> 11 visual arts professions: Graphic Designer, Video Editor, Cartoonist, Textile Designer, Painter, Sculptor, Ceramicist, Photographer, Cultural Officer, Medical Illustrator, Investigative Illustrator. Art skills apply across creative, scientific, and investigative fields.\n</div>\n  ",
