    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Drawing the <span class=\"learn-keyword\">human figure</span> is one of the most challenging and rewarding disciplines in visual arts. It requires understanding human anatomy, proportions, and the structural forms that underlie the body.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Human Proportions</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The standard adult human figure is approximately <strong>7–8 heads tall</strong>. The head is used as the unit of measurement:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>The navel is approximately at the halfway point (4 heads from top)</li>\n  <li>The hands reach mid-thigh when arms hang at sides</li>\n  <li>The knees are at approximately 5.5 heads from the top</li>\n  <li>The span of outstretched arms equals the height of the body</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Basic Forms of the Human Figure</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Head:</strong> Egg/sphere shape</li>\n  <li><strong>Trunk:</strong> Egg or cylindrical form (tapers from shoulders to waist)</li>\n  <li><strong>Arms and legs:</strong> Cylinders</li>\n  <li><strong>Hands and feet:</strong> Simplified wedge shapes initially</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. The Stick Figure Method</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">A quick method to establish pose and proportion — using lines to represent the spine, limbs, and centre of gravity before developing full forms.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Action Poses</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Human figures in action (running, jumping, throwing) have different proportion relationships because of foreshortening — parts of the body appearing compressed when pointed toward the viewer.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Adult human figure = 7–8 heads tall. Head = sphere/egg. Trunk = egg/cylinder. Arms/legs = cylinders. Hands/feet = wedge shapes. Navel = halfway point of the body. Arm span = body height.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Human figure proportion: 7–8 heads tall. Basic forms: head (sphere), trunk (egg/cylinder), limbs (cylinders). Stick figure = establish pose first. Foreshortening = compressed appearance of limbs pointing toward viewer.\n</div>\n  ",
