    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Art appreciation</span> is the understanding and enjoyment of art through critical observation, analysis, and evaluation. It involves developing the ability to look at art meaningfully and respond thoughtfully to what we see.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Art Appreciation</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Art appreciation is the process of understanding, evaluating, and enjoying artworks. It involves looking beyond the surface to understand an artwork's meaning, technique, historical context, and emotional impact.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Levels of Art Appreciation</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Description:</strong> What can you see? Identify the subject matter, colours, shapes, and elements without judging.</li>\n  <li><strong>Analysis:</strong> How is it made? Examine how the elements and principles of art are used — composition, colour relationships, line quality, texture.</li>\n  <li><strong>Interpretation:</strong> What does it mean? What ideas, emotions, or messages does the artwork communicate?</li>\n  <li><strong>Judgement:</strong> Is it successful? Evaluate the artwork's quality, effectiveness, and significance.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Elements of Art</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">The building blocks used to create art: Line, Shape, Form, Colour, Texture, Space, Value (Tone).</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">4. Principles of Art</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">How elements are organised: Balance, Contrast, Emphasis, Harmony, Movement, Pattern, Proportion, Rhythm, Unity.</p>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Four levels of appreciation: Description (WHAT you see), Analysis (HOW it's made), Interpretation (WHAT it means), Judgement (HOW WELL it works). Elements of art: Line, Shape, Form, Colour, Texture, Space, Value. Principles: Balance, Contrast, Emphasis, Harmony, Movement, Pattern, Proportion, Rhythm, Unity.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Art appreciation = understanding and enjoying art through critical observation. Four levels: Description, Analysis, Interpretation, Judgement. Elements of art (7): Line, Shape, Form, Colour, Texture, Space, Value. Principles (9): Balance, Contrast, Emphasis, Harmony, Movement, Pattern, Proportion, Rhythm, Unity.\n</div>\n  ",
