    "topic": "Introduction to Graphics I",
    "topicCode": "SS1-VA-11",
    "module": "Graphic Arts",
    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Graphics</span> is the art and science of visual communication — conveying information through images, symbols, text, and visual design. It encompasses everything from hand-drawn illustrations to digital design.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Graphics</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Graphics is the creation of visual communication materials using images, typography, and design to convey messages to specific audiences. It serves informational, commercial, and aesthetic purposes.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Types of Graphics</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Advertising Graphics:</strong> Posters, billboards, flyers, magazine ads designed to sell products or services.</li>\n  <li><strong>Editorial Graphics:</strong> Illustrations for newspapers, books, and magazines.</li>\n  <li><strong>Packaging Design:</strong> Visual design on product packaging (boxes, bottles, wrappers).</li>\n  <li><strong>Signage and Wayfinding:</strong> Signs, symbols, and directional graphics.</li>\n  <li><strong>Digital Graphics:</strong> Websites, social media graphics, digital advertisements.</li>\n  <li><strong>Identity/Branding:</strong> Logos, corporate identity systems.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Elements of Graphic Design</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Typography</td><td>The art of selecting and arranging typefaces (fonts) for readability and aesthetic effect</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Colour</td><td>Creates mood, attracts attention, and conveys brand identity</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Layout/Composition</td><td>Arrangement of visual elements on the page/screen</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Illustration</td><td>Hand-drawn or digital visual images</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Photography</td><td>Photographic images used in design</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Graphics = visual communication through images, typography, and design. Types: Advertising, Editorial, Packaging, Signage, Digital, Identity/Branding. Elements: Typography, Colour, Layout, Illustration, Photography.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Graphics = art of visual communication. Types include advertising, editorial, packaging, signage, digital, branding. Key elements: typography, colour, layout/composition, illustration, photography.\n</div>\n  ",
