    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  This topic deepens understanding of graphics by exploring <span class=\"learn-keyword\">lettering</span> and <span class=\"learn-keyword\">calligraphy</span> — the art of beautiful writing — alongside the principles that make graphic communication effective.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Lettering in Graphics</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Lettering is the art of drawing and designing letters. It differs from typography (selecting pre-made fonts) in that lettering involves custom-drawn letter forms.</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Roman lettering:</strong> Classic serif letterforms based on ancient Roman inscriptions — formal, authoritative.</li>\n  <li><strong>Gothic/Black Letter:</strong> Medieval style with thick, angular strokes — decorative and ornate.</li>\n  <li><strong>Italic:</strong> Slanted, flowing letterforms — informal, elegant.</li>\n  <li><strong>Sans-serif:</strong> Letters without serifs — clean, modern, and easily readable.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Calligraphy</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Calligraphy is the art of beautiful, decorative handwriting using specialist tools (nib pens, brushes). It has a long tradition in Arabic, Chinese, and Western cultures. Key features:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Thick and thin strokes created by pen angle and pressure.</li>\n  <li>Rhythm and consistency in letter spacing and proportions.</li>\n  <li>Used in formal documents, wedding invitations, religious manuscripts.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Principles of Good Lettering</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Legibility:</strong> Letters must be clear and easy to read.</li>\n  <li><strong>Proportion:</strong> Consistent size relationships between letter parts.</li>\n  <li><strong>Spacing:</strong> Consistent, appropriate space between letters and words.</li>\n  <li><strong>Alignment:</strong> Letters aligned on a consistent baseline.</li>\n  <li><strong>Unity:</strong> Consistent style throughout the lettering.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Lettering = art of drawing letters. Four lettering styles: Roman (serif, formal), Gothic/Black Letter (ornate, angular), Italic (slanted, flowing), Sans-serif (clean, modern). Calligraphy = beautiful decorative handwriting with thick/thin strokes. Principles: legibility, proportion, spacing, alignment, unity.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Lettering = custom-drawn letter design. Styles: Roman, Gothic, Italic, Sans-serif. Calligraphy = beautiful handwriting art (thick/thin strokes). Principles of good lettering: legibility, proportion, spacing, alignment, unity.\n</div>\n  ",
