    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Beyond print, advertising exists across many media — from large outdoor displays to electronic and digital platforms. This topic explores outdoor and electronic forms of graphic advertisement.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Outdoor Advertisement Forms</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Form</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Billboard/Hoarding</strong></td><td>Very large outdoor structure displaying advertisements along roads and in public spaces</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Banners</strong></td><td>Flexible printed signs hung across streets, buildings, or at events</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Signpost</strong></td><td>Signs on posts directing people and advertising businesses at roads</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Vehicle/Transit ads</strong></td><td>Advertisements printed on buses, taxis, trucks — mobile advertising</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Shopfront/Fascia boards</strong></td><td>Signs on the exterior of shops identifying the business</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Electronic and Digital Advertisement Forms</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Television advertisement (commercial):</strong> Moving image and sound for TV viewing.</li>\n  <li><strong>Electronic billboard/LED display:</strong> Digital screens displaying changing advertisements in public spaces.</li>\n  <li><strong>Online/Digital ads:</strong> Banner ads, social media ads, pop-ups on websites.</li>\n  <li><strong>Radio advertisement:</strong> Audio-only advertising (not strictly visual, but often uses graphic jingles/designs).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Design Principles for Outdoor Advertising</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Simplicity:</strong> Very limited text (7 words maximum ideal for billboards).</li>\n  <li><strong>Bold imagery:</strong> Large, simple, striking images visible from a distance.</li>\n  <li><strong>High contrast:</strong> Dark background/light text or vice versa for maximum visibility.</li>\n  <li><strong>Large typography:</strong> Fonts must be large and bold enough to read at speed.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Outdoor ads: Billboard/Hoarding, Banners, Signpost, Vehicle/Transit, Shopfront. Electronic: TV commercial, Electronic billboard, Online/digital ads. Billboard principle: minimal text (max 7 words), bold imagery, high contrast, large typography.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Outdoor ads: Billboard, Banners, Signpost, Vehicle transit, Shopfront. Electronic ads: TV, LED billboard, Online/digital. Outdoor design: simplicity, bold imagery, high contrast, large type.\n</div>\n  ",
