    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Computer graphics</span> is the use of computer software and digital tools to create, edit, and manipulate visual images. It has revolutionised the visual arts and design industry.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Computer Graphics</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Computer graphics refers to the creation and manipulation of visual content using computer hardware (mouse, graphic tablet, screen) and software (design programs). It encompasses both 2D and 3D visual creation.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Types of Computer Graphics</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Raster (Bitmap) graphics:</strong> Images made of pixels (tiny coloured squares). Resolution-dependent — loses quality when enlarged. Examples: Photographs, scanned images. Software: Photoshop, GIMP.</li>\n  <li><strong>Vector graphics:</strong> Images defined by mathematical paths/equations (lines, curves). Resolution-independent — scales to any size without losing quality. Software: Illustrator, CorelDRAW, Inkscape. Examples: Logos, illustrations.</li>\n  <li><strong>3D computer graphics:</strong> Three-dimensional models created digitally. Software: Blender, Maya, 3ds Max. Used in: films, video games, architecture.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Common Software Applications</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Software</th><th>Primary Use</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Adobe Photoshop</td><td>Photo editing and raster image creation</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Adobe Illustrator</td><td>Vector illustration and logo design</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>CorelDRAW</td><td>Vector graphics and layout design</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Canva</td><td>Simple web-based graphic design</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Blender</td><td>3D modelling and animation</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Two main types: Raster (pixel-based, loses quality when enlarged — Photoshop) and Vector (path-based, scales without quality loss — Illustrator, CorelDRAW). Vector best for logos. Raster best for photographs. Know the software: Photoshop (photo), Illustrator (vector), CorelDRAW (vector/layout), Blender (3D).\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Computer graphics = creating visual content with computers. Types: Raster (pixels, resolution-dependent) and Vector (paths, resolution-independent). Software: Photoshop (raster), Illustrator/CorelDRAW (vector), Blender (3D).\n</div>\n  ",
