    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  This topic extends computer graphics knowledge to include <span class=\"learn-keyword\">digital colour systems</span>, <span class=\"learn-keyword\">file formats</span>, and practical applications of computer graphics in visual arts practice.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Colour Models in Computer Graphics</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>RGB (Red, Green, Blue):</strong> Additive colour model used for screens and digital displays. Colours are created by combining light. RGB values range from 0–255. White = RGB(255,255,255); Black = RGB(0,0,0).</li>\n  <li><strong>CMYK (Cyan, Magenta, Yellow, Black):</strong> Subtractive colour model used in printing. Colours are created by subtracting light using inks. Used for professional print output.</li>\n  <li><strong>HSB/HSL (Hue, Saturation, Brightness/Lightness):</strong> Intuitive colour model describing colour in terms of hue (colour type), saturation (intensity), and brightness.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Common File Formats</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Format</th><th>Type</th><th>Best Use</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>JPEG/JPG</td><td>Raster</td><td>Photographs for web/print (compressed)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>PNG</td><td>Raster</td><td>Web graphics with transparency</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>GIF</td><td>Raster</td><td>Simple animations and web graphics</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>SVG</td><td>Vector</td><td>Scalable web graphics and logos</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>PDF</td><td>Both</td><td>Print-ready documents</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>PSD</td><td>Raster</td><td>Photoshop working files</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>AI</td><td>Vector</td><td>Adobe Illustrator working files</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Applications of Computer Graphics in Nigeria</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Designing naira currency and government documents</li>\n  <li>Creating Nollywood movie posters and cover art</li>\n  <li>Designing logos for Nigerian businesses</li>\n  <li>Creating advertisements for Nigerian products</li>\n  <li>Architectural visualisation for building projects</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> RGB = screen/digital (additive, light). CMYK = print/ink (subtractive). File formats: JPEG (compressed photos), PNG (transparency, web), SVG (scalable vector), PDF (print-ready), PSD (Photoshop), AI (Illustrator). RGB for screens; CMYK for professional printing.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Colour models: RGB (screens) and CMYK (print). File formats: JPEG/PNG (raster), SVG (vector), PDF (print), PSD/AI (working files). Computer graphics used widely in Nigeria: currency, Nollywood, advertising, logos.\n</div>\n  ",
