    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">Textile design</span> is the creation of patterns and designs for fabric. It is both a fine and applied art with a rich tradition in Nigerian culture, from the adire of the Yoruba to the akwete weaving of the Igbo.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Meaning of Textile Design</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Textile design is the art of creating patterns, motifs, and designs for fabric through weaving, printing, dyeing, or embroidery. The designs may be functional (clothing) or decorative (wall hangings).</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Types of Textile Design Techniques</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Technique</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Weaving</strong></td><td>Interlacing warp and weft threads to create patterned fabric</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Dyeing</strong></td><td>Applying colour to fabric using natural or synthetic dyes</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Batik</strong></td><td>Resist-dyeing technique using wax to block dye from areas of fabric</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Tie-Dye (Adire)</strong></td><td>Binding, folding, or stitching fabric before dyeing to create patterns</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Screen Printing</strong></td><td>Pushing ink through a mesh screen onto fabric</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Embroidery</strong></td><td>Decorating fabric with needle and thread</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Nigerian Traditional Textiles</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Adire (Yoruba):</strong> Indigo-dyed cloth using tie-dye or starch-resist technique.</li>\n  <li><strong>Aso-oke (Yoruba):</strong> Hand-woven strip cloth used for traditional ceremonies.</li>\n  <li><strong>Akwete (Igbo):</strong> Hand-woven cloth from Akwete, Abia State — distinctive geometric patterns.</li>\n  <li><strong>Kijipa (Hausa):</strong> Hand-woven cotton cloth with striped patterns.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Techniques: Weaving (warp/weft), Dyeing, Batik (wax resist), Tie-dye/Adire (binding before dye), Screen printing, Embroidery. Nigerian textiles: Adire (Yoruba, indigo), Aso-oke (Yoruba, woven strips), Akwete (Igbo, geometric weave), Kijipa (Hausa, striped cotton).\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Textile design = patterns for fabric by weaving, dyeing, batik, tie-dye, screen printing, embroidery. Nigerian textiles: Adire (Yoruba), Aso-oke (Yoruba), Akwete (Igbo), Kijipa (Hausa).\n</div>\n  ",
