    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  This topic extends textile design knowledge to include principles of <span class=\"learn-keyword\">pattern creation</span>, <span class=\"learn-keyword\">colour in textiles</span>, and the design process for creating original textile patterns.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Principles of Pattern Design</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Motif:</strong> The basic unit or decorative element that forms the foundation of a pattern.</li>\n  <li><strong>Repetition:</strong> The motif repeated across the fabric surface.</li>\n  <li><strong>Rhythm:</strong> Visual movement created by the regular or varied repetition of motifs.</li>\n  <li><strong>Symmetry:</strong> Balance achieved by mirroring motifs — bilateral, radial, or translational.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Types of Pattern Arrangement</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>All-over pattern:</strong> The motif repeats uniformly across the entire fabric surface.</li>\n  <li><strong>Border pattern:</strong> The pattern runs along the edges of the fabric only.</li>\n  <li><strong>Spot pattern:</strong> Isolated motifs placed at intervals on the fabric.</li>\n  <li><strong>Stripe pattern:</strong> Repeated lines of colour or texture running the length/width of fabric.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Colour in Textile Design</h3>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Colour harmony:</strong> Pleasing combinations using complementary, analogous, or monochromatic schemes.</li>\n  <li><strong>Natural dyes:</strong> From plants, minerals, insects — giving organic, earthy tones.</li>\n  <li><strong>Synthetic dyes:</strong> Chemical dyes — bright, consistent, wide colour range.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Motif = basic unit of pattern. Pattern types: All-over (covers all fabric), Border (edges only), Spot (isolated motifs), Stripe (lines). Symmetry: bilateral (left/right), radial (from centre), translational (repeated shifts).\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Pattern elements: motif, repetition, rhythm, symmetry. Pattern types: all-over, border, spot, stripe. Colour: harmonious combinations, natural dyes (organic), synthetic dyes (bright, consistent).\n</div>\n  ",
