    "term": "Second Term",
    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  <span class=\"learn-keyword\">3-dimensional (3D) art</span> includes all art forms that occupy physical space — sculpture, ceramics, architecture, and installation art. These works can be viewed from multiple angles and have real depth.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Key 3D Art Terms</h3>\n<div class=\"learn-table-wrap\">\n  <table class=\"learn-table\">\n    <thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Definition</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td><strong>Relief sculpture</strong></td><td>Sculpture that projects from a flat background — figures emerge from the surface</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Low relief (bas-relief)</strong></td><td>Slight projection from the background (e.g., coins, Benin bronze plaques)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>High relief</strong></td><td>Strong projection — figures project significantly from the background</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Sculpture in the round</strong></td><td>Free-standing sculpture viewable from all sides</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Armature</strong></td><td>The internal wire/metal framework supporting a clay or other sculpted form</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Kiln</strong></td><td>A high-temperature oven used to fire ceramics</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Glaze</strong></td><td>A liquid glass-like coating applied to ceramics before firing to create a sealed, coloured surface</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Casting</strong></td><td>Pouring molten metal or liquid material into a mould to create a sculpture</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Modelling</strong></td><td>Building up form by adding material (clay, wax)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td><strong>Carving</strong></td><td>Removing material from a solid block to reveal form</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> 3D art occupies real space, viewable from multiple angles. Relief: low (slight, coins/bronze plaques) vs high (strong projection). Sculpture in the round = free-standing. Modelling = adding material. Carving = removing material. Armature = internal wire support. Kiln = fires ceramics.\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> 3D art = occupies real space. Relief sculpture: low relief (coins) vs high relief. Sculpture in the round = free-standing. Armature = wire support. Kiln fires ceramics. Glaze = coating. Casting = mould. Modelling (add) vs Carving (remove).\n</div>\n  ",
