    "contentHTML": "\n<div class=\"learn-intro\">\n  Continuing the study of modelling, this topic focuses on <span class=\"learn-keyword\">figure modelling</span> — building the human form in clay — and the <span class=\"learn-keyword\">relief modelling</span> tradition in Nigerian art.\n</div>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">1. Figure Modelling</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Modelling the human figure in clay requires the same understanding of human proportions as drawing:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>The figure is 7–8 heads tall.</li>\n  <li>Build on an armature (wire skeleton) for standing figures.</li>\n  <li>Block in main masses (head, torso, limbs) before refining details.</li>\n  <li>Work from general to specific — overall form first, details last.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">2. Relief Modelling</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Relief modelling creates forms that project from a flat background. Steps:</p>\n<ol class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li>Prepare a flat clay slab as the background.</li>\n  <li>Plan the composition by drawing or pressing the design into the clay.</li>\n  <li>Build up the forms — the highest relief areas receive the most additional clay.</li>\n  <li>Refine edges and surfaces.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<h3 class=\"learn-subheading\">3. Nigerian Relief Modelling Tradition</h3>\n<p class=\"learn-p\">Relief modelling has a long tradition in Nigeria:</p>\n<ul class=\"learn-list\">\n  <li><strong>Benin bronze plaques:</strong> Cast bronze low-relief panels depicting court ceremonies and warriors.</li>\n  <li><strong>Ife terracotta heads:</strong> High naturalistic modelling in clay.</li>\n  <li><strong>Yoruba relief on palace doors:</strong> Carved wood and cast bronze relief panels.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">💡</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Figure modelling: use armature + work general to specific. Relief modelling: flat clay slab background + build up forms. Nigerian tradition: Benin bronze plaques (cast low-relief), Ife terracotta (naturalistic modelling), Yoruba palace doors (relief panels).\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"learn-tip-box\">\n  <span class=\"learn-tip-icon\">🎯</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Figure modelling: armature + proportions (7–8 heads). Relief: flat slab background + add clay for projection. Nigerian relief: Benin bronze plaques, Ife terracotta, Yoruba palace doors.\n</div>\n  ",
