      {"q": "Nok culture discovery has been called a 'missing link' in African art history because:", "o": ["It connects Nigerian art to European traditions", "It proves West Africa had sophisticated sculpture long before European contact", "It proved all African art came from Egypt", "Nok artists trained in Rome"], "a": 1, "e": "Nok fills a historical gap — demonstrating West Africa had its own sophisticated indigenous sculptural tradition from at least 500 BC, independent of external influence.", "h": "Nok = 'missing link' — West Africa's own ancient indigenous sculpture.", "yr": "SS1"},
      {"q": "Both Nok and Ife traditions are important to Nigerian identity because:", "o": ["They were made for European collectors", "They demonstrate Nigeria's ancient, sophisticated artistic heritage — foundational to national pride", "They are Nigeria's only art traditions", "They were recently discovered with no historical depth"], "a": 1, "e": "Nok and Ife are foundational to Nigerian cultural identity — demonstrating thousands of years of sophisticated indigenous art before colonialism.", "h": "Nok + Ife = foundational to Nigerian cultural identity.", "yr": "SS1"},
      {"q": "Ife portrait heads were used in which context?", "o": ["Architectural decoration", "Royal ceremonies and ancestor veneration to honour deceased rulers", "Trade goods exported to Europe", "Children's toys"], "a": 1, "e": "Ife portrait heads were placed on shrines and used in royal ceremonies for ancestor veneration — honouring deceased rulers of Ife.", "h": "Ife heads: royal ceremonies + ancestor veneration.", "yr": "SS1"},
      {"q": "The approximate period of Ife artistic production was:", "o": ["500 BC – 200 AD", "9th–15th century AD", "1600–1900 AD", "1800–present"], "a": 1, "e": "The height of Ife artistic production dates to approximately the 9th–15th centuries AD.", "h": "Ife art period: 9th–15th century AD.", "yr": "SS1"},
      {"q": "What is the correct chronological order of these traditions (oldest first)?", "o": ["Ife → Nok → Benin", "Benin → Ife → Nok", "Nok → Ife → Benin", "Ife → Benin → Nok"], "a": 2, "e": "Nok (500 BC–200 AD) is oldest, then Ife (9th–15th century), then Benin (13th century+).", "h": "Oldest to newest: Nok → Ife → Benin.", "yr": "SS1"}
